      "writtenOn": "2024-06-25T08:44:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "- Add a constant `FD_MAX_WAIT_NANOS \u003d 1000000000` or similar and use it here? The reason is that I\u0027m not sure if it will be obvious to the reader that this is in nanoseconds.\n- What\u0027s the reason for choosing one second here?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1266,
        "startChar": 36,
        "endLine": 1266,
        "endChar": 46
      },
      "revId": "67ac93dca17393bf0fc8e0758c3e34d2f6ec5557",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ac1c0bfa_18e33f43",
        "filename": "media/libstagefright/MPEG4Writer.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1266,
      "author": {
        "id": 3263990
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-06-27T06:36:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It is possible that the application hasn\u0027t set the file descriptor even after an approaching file size. In this case, it should still fail as before and not wait indefinitely hence the timeout. While debugging this issue on Shiba we observed that the delay in handling the \u0027setNextFd\u0027 message from application was always less than 1 second. So, we have used this value for timeout.",
      "parentUuid": "2a95636d_ff4c8d5b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1266,
        "startChar": 36,
        "endLine": 1266,
        "endChar": 46
      },
      "revId": "67ac93dca17393bf0fc8e0758c3e34d2f6ec5557",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5757b481_f4420137",
        "filename": "media/libstagefright/MPEG4Writer.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1266,
      "author": {
        "id": 1060104
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-06-27T08:00:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For the benefit of a future reader of the code, I think it\u0027s useful to document the rationale for choosing a timeout value like this (even the documentation says it\u0027s arbitrary) as it can help them understand constraints in case they need to change it in future. Please add a comment (maybe something like \"Allow up to 1 second, which is safely above the maximum delay observed in manual testing between posting from setNextFd and handling it\" if that\u0027s accurate?).\n\nBy the way, I\u0027m surprised the required delay is as large as one second. It makes me wonder whether there is some expensive operation that regularly blocks handling this message for longer periods of time (possibly even longer than 1 second). Would a delay of say 100 ms work? The reason to keep the timeout small is that it sounds like some use cases do actually rely on reaching this delay (app hasn\u0027t set an FD when approaching the file size).",
      "parentUuid": "ac1c0bfa_18e33f43",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1266,
        "startChar": 36,
        "endLine": 1266,
        "endChar": 46
      },
      "revId": "67ac93dca17393bf0fc8e0758c3e34d2f6ec5557",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
